  "narration": "Central banks are not printing money anymore. The government is. The Fed isn't leading the market. It is chasing a moving tiger. For a decade, we believed low rates were the only engine of growth. Investors grew addicted to cheap debt and artificial stability. But in the current cycle, the engine changed. Fiscal dominance arrived. Governments are now bypassing banks to inject capital directly into the economy. Inflation is a policy choice, not an accident of the supply chain. Zombie companies are dying because their 2% debt is now a trap. Real assets win when the currency is devalued to fund deficits. Wealth is being redistributed from the saver to the spender. The risk is no longer a crash. It is a slow, hot burn. The printing press hasn't stopped. It just found a new operator.",

